  "sourceRef": "SARS PAYE-GEN-01-G21 (2027) Rev 1 p. 31-32 (leave pay on termination taxed as a bonus, 3605); Magistrates' Courts Act 32 of 1944 s61 ('emoluments'), s65J(1)(b)(i), s65J(1A)(a); Maintenance Act 99 of 1998 s1 ('emoluments'), s28(1), s29(3) (Juta consolidations on justice.gov.za, read 2026-11-26); Hein rulings 6 and 15 (wave 7)",
  "notes": "Breaker #1939 H1. As termination-garnishee-severance-excluded (R10 000 leave pay, R50 000 severance 3901), with a R9 000 maintenance order (Maintenance Act s28(1), s29(3): outside the 25%). The severance carries nil PAYE (no directive is modelled, which costs it as a nil directive would: the R550 000 tax-free severance band), so every rand of the line's PAYE (2192.00, the leave pay as a 3605 annual payment) and UIF (nil) is the leave pay's. The leave pay nets 10 000 - 2 192 = 7 808.00, and that is all the order may take (ruling 6: severance never attached): 7 808.00 of R9 000, the rest owed. Net 60 000 - 2 192 - 7 808 = 50 000.00, the severance untouched. A net x base / gross split would take 57 808 x 10 000 / 60 000 = 9 000 (R1 192 of severance).",
